        "curated_prompt": "ROLLUP generates incorrect SQL with CUBE instead of ROLLUP\n\n#### Description\n\nWhen using the `rollup()` method on queries, the generated SQL contains `WITH CUBE` instead of the expected `WITH ROLLUP`.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nfrom pypika import Query, Table\n\ntable = Table('abc')\nq = Query.from_(table).select(table.foo).rollup(table.foo, vendor='mysql')\nprint(str(q))\n```\n\n**Expected output:**\n```sql\nSELECT \"foo\" FROM \"abc\" GROUP BY \"foo\" WITH ROLLUP\n```\n\n**Actual output:**\n```sql\nSELECT \"foo\" FROM \"abc\" GROUP BY \"foo\" WITH CUBE\n```\n\nThe reproduction above exercises the vendor=\"mysql\" path that emits a WITH ROLLUP clause. The generated SQL should use WITH ROLLUP for that path.\n",
